<title>USA: Geriatric &amp; Medical Q4 shr $0.03 vs $0.07.</title>
<headline>Geriatric &amp; Medical Q4 shr $0.03 vs $0.07.</headline>
<dateline>PHILADELPHIA 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>GERIATRIC &amp; MEDICAL COMPANIES, INC.</p>
<p>		     CONSOLIDATED STATEMENTS OF OPERATIONS</p>
<p>			   FOR THE THREE MONTHS AND TWELVE MONTHS</p>
<p>		   ENDED MAY 31, 1996, AND 1995</p>
<p>		    (IN THOUSANDS EXCEPT PER SHARE AMOUNTS)</p>
<p>					Three Months Ended  Years Ended</p>
<p>						 May 31,	May 31,</p>
<p>				   1996(A)     1995  1996(A)     1995</p>
<p> Operating revenues, net    $47,095 $49,912 $195,196 $192,234</p>
<p>				     47,095  49,912  195,196  192,234</p>
<p>Expenses:</p>
<p> Operating expenses	    42,186  42,969  167,060  163,769</p>
<p>Depreciation and amortization</p>
<p>					1,990   2,344    8,778    8,734</p>
<p> Interest expense, net	  3,718   2,918   12,295   11,078</p>
<p>Provision for costs on sale</p>
<p>   of accounts receivable     1,061     334    4,170    3,588</p>
<p>				     48,955  48,565  192,303  187,169</p>
<p>Income (loss) before</p>
<p>   income taxes		 (1,860)   1,347    2,893    5,065</p>
<p>Income tax provision (benefit)</p>
<p>				    (2,356)     267  (1,260)    1,012</p>
<p> Net Income			   496   1,080    4,153    4,053</p>
<p>Earnings per common share:</p>
<p> Net Income			  0.03    0.07     0.27     0.27</p>
<p> Average Shares Outstanding  15,372  15,209   15,372   15,209</p>
<p>NOTE: Full company name is Geriatric &amp; Medical Cos Inc.</p>
<p>(A) The fourth quarter and 12 months ended May 31, 1996, reflect the recording of a charge pertaining to the settlement of a 1992 class-action suit; additional provision for bad debts totalling $1,750,000; additional interest expense of $621,000 required under a mortgage agreement; a $500,000 prepayment discount on a note receivable; and recognition of a deferred tax asset. The after-tax effect of these items was $918,000 in the fourth quarter.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
